  "body": "Modern, beautifully renovated and surprisingly spacious, 9/101 Brightside Road, Stanmore Bay presents an exciting opportunity for working couples, astute investors, young families, first-home buyers or those seeking the perfect retirement option.\r\n\r\nTucked away within a quiet, gated complex, this appealing three-bedroom end townhouse with ample storage combines privacy, security and easy-care living. Enjoy its sunny aspect and abundance of natural light, with the added bonus of being freshly painted throughout and featuring new flooring, creating a fresh, modern feel that's ready for you to simply move in and enjoy.\r\n\r\nThe welcoming open-plan living area creates the perfect space to relax or entertain, while the gorgeous spacious private courtyard offers a peaceful garden retreat - ideal for morning coffee, alfresco dining or soaking up the sunshine. There's also loads of storage throughout, making everyday living that much easier.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the master bedroom features an oversized wardrobe and its own private balcony, providing a lovely spot to unwind. Two additional bedrooms offer flexibility for family, guests or hobbies. An upgraded bathroom and separate toilet add everyday convenience, while the single internal-access garage provides secure parking and extra practicality.\r\n\r\nAnd the location is hard to beat! Stroll to nearby cafes, restaurants and the supermarket, or enjoy an easy wander down to Stanmore Bay Beach for a refreshing swim. With local amenities close at hand, you can embrace a relaxed, holiday-inspired lifestyle every day.\r\n\r\nWhether you're searching for a smart investment, a stylish first home, a comfortable retirement option or a low-maintenance lock-up-and-leave, this property offers space, convenience and coastal appeal without the upkeep of a larger home.\r\n\r\nThree bedrooms, sunshine, fresh modern finishes and a superb coastal location - this is easy-care living at its best. Come and see it for yourself before someone else snaps it up!\r\n\r\nDeadline Sale Closes: 4:00pm, Thursday 19 November 2026 (unless sold prior)",
